proof_plan:
At $\sigma^*$, some pure action $a$ used by player $i$ has $\map {u_i} {a, \sigma_{-i}^*} \le \map {u_i} {\sigma^*}$, so $\map {c_{i, a} } {\sigma^*} = 0$, which forces $\sum_b \map {c_{i, b} } {\sigma^*} = 0$.
Hence no player has a profitable deviation, and $\sigma^*$ is a [[Definition:Nash Equilibrium|Nash equilibrium]].
{{qed}}
